Recoil [
    Title: "Brom zero-latency true-stereo convolver"
    Description: {
        Convolves a stereo signal with a true-stereo impulse response: four
        paths, L->L, L->R, R->L and R->R, up to the capacity given at create.
        Zero latency, f64 throughout, no threads, and deterministic, so an
        offline bounce is bit-identical to a realtime one.

        Layout of the impulse response:

            taps [0, 128)           direct-form FIR, per sample
            taps [128, 2048)        level 0: 30 partitions of 64
            taps [2048, 16384)      level 1: 14 partitions of 1024
            taps [16384, 65536)     level 2: 6 partitions of 8192
            taps [65536, capacity)  level 3: partitions of 32768

        Every level is a uniformly partitioned overlap-save convolver whose
        work for one block is spread evenly over the 64-sample ticks of the
        following block. A level of partition size P whose first tap sits at
        2P has exactly one block period in which to finish, which is why each
        level starts at twice its own size (Gardner 1995, with the work
        scheduled by tick count rather than a worker thread). Level 0's block
        is a single tick, so it does its whole block at once; the direct head
        is 128 taps rather than 64 so that level 0 obeys the same rule and
        needs no special case.

        The cost per sample stays flat because no level does a whole block's
        work in one tick. The largest single unit is one 65536-point real FFT,
        which is why the top level stops at 32768.

        Changing the impulse response is time-sliced too. `brom-conv-stage-*`
        transforms the new response into the spare partition set a few FFTs
        per call; once complete, each level crosses over at its own next block
        boundary. It computes both outputs for one block and fades between
        them over the next one, so the early part changes within milliseconds
        and the far tail follows within one top-level period (65536 samples,
        under 1.5 s at 44.1 kHz) -- by which time it is only now being heard.

        Memory is allocated once at create for the capacity, two partition sets
        (live and spare) plus the frequency-domain delay line, about 24 bytes
        per tap of capacity per path pair: roughly 185 MB for 20 s at 48 kHz
        including the caller's time-domain staging copy. The audio path
        never allocates.

        Ownership. std/math/fft takes an `rfft-plan!` value and `vector!
        [f64!]` buffers, both refcounted, while everything else here is raw
        memory. Each level keeps its plan and the vectors that cross the
        FFT call (time frame, the two input snapshots, a spectrum pair) as
        fields of its `conv-level!` record, and the records themselves live
        in one `vector! [conv-level!]` that the state owns as a raw pointer.
        Field stores into a record are plain moves, and releasing that one
        vector at destroy runs the compiler's element drop on every record,
        which releases each plan and vector exactly once. The delay line,
        the partition spectra and the accumulators stay raw; a transform's
        result is copied into its slot from the spectrum pair, and an
        accumulator into the pair before the inverse, since the inverse
        overwrites the spectrum it is given.
    }
    Type: module
    Module: brom/dsp/convolver
    Imports: [
        std/math/fft [rfft-plan! rfft-plan rfft-forward rfft-inverse]
    ]
    Exports: [
        BROM-CONV-TICK BROM-CONV-HEAD BROM-CONV-HEAD-FADE
        brom-conv-create brom-conv-destroy brom-conv-reset brom-conv-clear brom-conv-capacity
        brom-conv-process brom-conv-length brom-conv-busy
        brom-conv-stage-begin brom-conv-stage-step brom-conv-staging
        brom-conv-memory-bytes
    ]
]

; The scheduler's tick, which is also level 0's partition size.
BROM-CONV-TICK: 64
; Direct-form head length: twice the tick, where level 0 starts.
BROM-CONV-HEAD: 128
; Samples over which the direct head crosses from the old response to the
; new. Every partitioned level fades over one of its own blocks.
BROM-CONV-HEAD-FADE: 1024
BROM-CONV-LEVELS: 4

; The four true-stereo paths, as input * 2 + output.
BROM-CONV-LL: 0
BROM-CONV-LR: 1
BROM-CONV-RL: 2
BROM-CONV-RR: 3

; Level phases around a response change.
CONV-PHASE-STEADY: 0
; This block computes outputs with both sets.
CONV-PHASE-DUAL: 1
; This block plays the two outputs computed last block, fading old to new.
CONV-PHASE-FADE: 2

conv-cell!: make c-struct! [value: [f64!]]

conv-level!: make c-struct! [
    lv-size: [i32!]
    lv-offset: [i32!]
    lv-max-parts: [i32!]
    lv-bins: [i32!]
    ; Ticks per block: lv-size / BROM-CONV-TICK. One for level 0.
    lv-ticks: [i32!]
    ; Owned by the record: released by the level store's element drop.
    lv-plan: [rfft-plan!]
    ; 2P input history per channel: [previous block | block being filled].
    lv-frame-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-frame-r: [c-pointer!]
    ; Copy of the frame at the boundary, so the second channel's FFT can run
    ; on a later tick while the frame keeps filling. Owned, 2P each.
    lv-snap-l: [vector! [f64!]]
    lv-snap-r: [vector! [f64!]]
    ; Spectrum of the transform just run, lv-bins each: a forward result
    ; waits here to be copied into its slot, and an accumulator is copied
    ; here to be inverted. Owned.
    lv-spec-re: [vector! [f64!]]
    lv-spec-im: [vector! [f64!]]
    ; Frequency-domain delay line: lv-max-parts slots of lv-bins per channel.
    lv-fdl-re-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-fdl-im-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-fdl-re-r: [c-pointer!]
    lv-fdl-im-r: [c-pointer!]
    lv-fdl-head: [i32!]
    ; Partition spectra, two sets: 4 paths x lv-max-parts x lv-bins each.
    lv-h-re-0: [c-pointer!]
    lv-h-im-0: [c-pointer!]
    lv-h-re-1: [c-pointer!]
    lv-h-im-1: [c-pointer!]
    ; Accumulators per output channel; -alt is the other set's during DUAL.
    lv-acc-re-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-acc-im-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-acc-re-r: [c-pointer!]
    lv-acc-im-r: [c-pointer!]
    lv-alt-re-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-alt-im-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-alt-re-r: [c-pointer!]
    lv-alt-im-r: [c-pointer!]
    ; 2P time frame: a staged partition's input, and an inverse's output.
    ; Owned.
    lv-time: [vector! [f64!]]
    ; Output being played this block, and being built for the next one. The
    ; -alt pair carries the second set's output across a crossover.
    lv-play-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-play-r: [c-pointer!]
    lv-play-alt-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-play-alt-r: [c-pointer!]
    lv-build-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-build-r: [c-pointer!]
    lv-build-alt-l: [c-pointer!]
    lv-build-alt-r: [c-pointer!]
    ; Position inside the current block, and the scheduler's state.
    lv-pos: [i32!]
    lv-tick: [i32!]
    lv-units: [i32!]
    lv-done: [i32!]
    ; Which set is live, the crossover phase, and whether this level has
    ; already crossed over to the pending set.
    lv-set: [i32!]
    lv-phase: [i32!]
    lv-switched: [logic!]
]

conv-state!: make c-struct! [
    cv-capacity: [i32!]
    ; The level records: an owned vector! [conv-level!], held as a raw
    ; pointer that carries its one reference until conv-release gives it
    ; back. cv-levels is that vector's data, which never moves.
    cv-level-store: [c-pointer!]
    cv-levels: [c-pointer!]
    ; Head taps, reversed, 4 paths x HEAD, two sets.
    cv-head-0: [c-pointer!]
    cv-head-1: [c-pointer!]
    ; 2 x HEAD input history per channel, written twice so the last HEAD
    ; samples are always contiguous.
    cv-hist-l: [c-pointer!]
    cv-hist-r: [c-pointer!]
    cv-hist-pos: [i32!]
    ; Samples since the last tick.
    cv-tick-pos: [i32!]
    ; Response length per set, in taps, and the live set.
    cv-length-0: [i32!]
    cv-length-1: [i32!]
    cv-set: [i32!]
    ; A complete response waits in the spare set to be crossed over to.
    cv-pending: [logic!]
    ; Samples left in the head and level-0 crossfade; zero when none runs.
    cv-head-fade: [i32!]
    ; Staging: the source paths (borrowed), their length, gain, and the
    ; next unit to transform.
    cv-staging: [logic!]
    cv-src-ll: [c-pointer!]
    cv-src-lr: [c-pointer!]
    cv-src-rl: [c-pointer!]
    cv-src-rr: [c-pointer!]
    cv-src-length: [i32!]
    cv-src-gain: [f64!]
    cv-stage-level: [i32!]
    cv-stage-path: [i32!]
    cv-stage-part: [i32!]
    cv-bytes: [i64!]
]

conv-get: func [
    #inline
    "Read one f64 from a raw buffer."
    :base [c-pointer!] "Borrowed buffer."
    index [i32!] "Element index."
    return: [f64!] "The element."
] [
    cell: make [#mutable conv-cell!] as conv-cell! (base + ((as u64! index) << 3))
    return cell/value
]

conv-put: func [
    #inline
    "Write one f64 into a raw buffer."
    :base [c-pointer!] "Borrowed buffer."
    index [i32!] "Element index."
    value [f64!] "Value to store."
    return: [none!]
] [
    cell: make [#mutable conv-cell!] as conv-cell! (base + ((as u64! index) << 3))
    cell/value: value
]

conv-at: func [
    #inline
    "Address of element `index` of an f64 buffer."
    :base [c-pointer!] "Borrowed buffer."
    index [i32!] "Element index."
    return: [c-pointer!] "Borrowed address inside the same buffer."
] [
    return base + ((as u64! index) << 3)
]

conv-alloc: func [
    "Allocate and zero `count` f64 values, adding their size to the state's tally."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state, for the byte tally."
    count [i32!] "Element count."
    return: [c-pointer!] "Owned buffer, or null when count is zero."
] [
    if count <= 0 [return as c-pointer! 0]
    raw: make c-pointer! unsafe/malloc (count * 8)
    unsafe/memset raw 0 (count * 8)
    state/cv-bytes: state/cv-bytes + (as i64! count) * 8
    return raw
]

conv-free: func [
    "Release a buffer from conv-alloc."
    :buffer [c-pointer!] "Owned buffer; null is ignored."
    return: [none!]
] [
    if buffer = as c-pointer! 0 [return none]
    unsafe/free buffer
]

conv-clear: func [
    "Zero `count` f64 values."
    :buffer [c-pointer!] "Borrowed buffer; null is ignored."
    count [i32!] "Element count."
    return: [none!]
] [
    if buffer = as c-pointer! 0 [return none]
    if count <= 0 [return none]
    unsafe/memset buffer 0 (count * 8)
    return none
]

conv-vector: func [
    "A zeroed, writable f64 vector of `count` elements, adding its size to the state's tally. Setup only: it allocates."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state, for the byte tally."
    count [i32!] "Element count."
    return: [vector! [f64!]] "Owned vector."
] [
    grow: make [#flexible vector! [f64!]] none
    repeat i count [append grow 0.0]
    state/cv-bytes: state/cv-bytes + (as i64! count) * 8
    return thaw freeze grow
]

conv-release: func [
    "Give back the level store's reference that brom-conv-create cast to a raw pointer. On the last one the store is freed, and its element drop releases every record's plan and vectors."
    :held [c-pointer!] "Owned raw reference to the store; null is ignored."
    return: [none!]
] [
    if held = as c-pointer! 0 [return none]
    store: as vector! held
    unused store
]

conv-level-view: func [
    #inline
    "Address of level `index`'s record."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    index [i32!] "Level 0 .. BROM-CONV-LEVELS-1."
    return: [c-pointer!] "Borrowed level record."
] [
    return state/cv-levels + (index * (as i32! size-of conv-level!))
]

conv-level-size: func [
    "Partition size of level `index`."
    index [i32!] "Level 0 .. BROM-CONV-LEVELS-1."
    return: [i32!] "64, 1024, 8192 or 32768."
] [
    if index = 0 [return 64]
    if index = 1 [return 1024]
    if index = 2 [return 8192]
    return 32768
]

conv-level-offset: func [
    "First tap level `index` covers."
    index [i32!] "Level 0 .. BROM-CONV-LEVELS-1."
    return: [i32!] "Tap offset: twice the level's partition size."
] [
    return 2 * (conv-level-size index)
]

conv-level-span: func [
    "Taps level `index` can cover at most: up to the next level's offset, or to capacity for the top level."
    index [i32!] "Level 0 .. BROM-CONV-LEVELS-1."
    capacity [i32!] "Convolver capacity in taps."
    return: [i32!] "Tap count; zero when capacity ends before this level starts."
] [
    start: conv-level-offset index
    stop: either index = (BROM-CONV-LEVELS - 1) [capacity] [conv-level-offset (index + 1)]
    limit: either stop < capacity [stop] [capacity]
    if limit <= start [return 0]
    return limit - start
]

conv-parts-for: func [
    "Partitions level `index` needs to cover a response of `length` taps."
    index [i32!] "Level 0 .. BROM-CONV-LEVELS-1."
    length [i32!] "Response length in taps."
    return: [i32!] "Partition count, possibly zero."
] [
    size: conv-level-size index
    span: conv-level-span index length
    if span <= 0 [return 0]
    return (span + size - 1) / size
]

brom-conv-create: func [
    "Allocate a convolver for responses up to `capacity` taps."
    capacity [i32!] "Longest response in taps, e.g. 20 s at the activation sample rate."
    return: [c-pointer!] "Owned convolver; release with brom-conv-destroy. Null for a non-positive capacity."
] [
    if capacity <= 0 [return as c-pointer! 0]
    raw: make c-pointer! unsafe/malloc (as i32! size-of conv-state!)
    unsafe/memset raw 0 (as i32! size-of conv-state!)
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! raw
    state/cv-capacity: capacity
    ; Zeroed records, one per level (4 is BROM-CONV-LEVELS; a vector's
    ; length must be written as a literal). The store's data is where they
    ; live.
    store: make [#mutable vector! [conv-level! 4]] []
    state/cv-levels: store/data
    ; The cast consumes `store`: its reference now belongs to the state,
    ; and conv-release gives it back at destroy.
    state/cv-level-store: as c-pointer! store
    state/cv-head-0: conv-alloc :state (4 * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    state/cv-head-1: conv-alloc :state (4 * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    state/cv-hist-l: conv-alloc :state (2 * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    state/cv-hist-r: conv-alloc :state (2 * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    repeat index BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
        lv: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index)
        size: conv-level-size index
        bins: size + 1
        parts: conv-parts-for index capacity
        lv/lv-size: size
        lv/lv-offset: conv-level-offset index
        lv/lv-max-parts: parts
        lv/lv-bins: bins
        lv/lv-ticks: size / BROM-CONV-TICK
        lv/lv-switched: true
        if parts > 0 [
            ; Stored straight from the call: a field store moves the plan in,
            ; where a local would hold an extra reference to its tables.
            lv/lv-plan: rfft-plan (2 * size)
            lv/lv-frame-l: conv-alloc :state (2 * size)
            lv/lv-frame-r: conv-alloc :state (2 * size)
            lv/lv-snap-l: conv-vector :state (2 * size)
            lv/lv-snap-r: conv-vector :state (2 * size)
            lv/lv-spec-re: conv-vector :state bins
            lv/lv-spec-im: conv-vector :state bins
            lv/lv-fdl-re-l: conv-alloc :state (parts * bins)
            lv/lv-fdl-im-l: conv-alloc :state (parts * bins)
            lv/lv-fdl-re-r: conv-alloc :state (parts * bins)
            lv/lv-fdl-im-r: conv-alloc :state (parts * bins)
            lv/lv-h-re-0: conv-alloc :state (4 * parts * bins)
            lv/lv-h-im-0: conv-alloc :state (4 * parts * bins)
            lv/lv-h-re-1: conv-alloc :state (4 * parts * bins)
            lv/lv-h-im-1: conv-alloc :state (4 * parts * bins)
            lv/lv-acc-re-l: conv-alloc :state bins
            lv/lv-acc-im-l: conv-alloc :state bins
            lv/lv-acc-re-r: conv-alloc :state bins
            lv/lv-acc-im-r: conv-alloc :state bins
            lv/lv-alt-re-l: conv-alloc :state bins
            lv/lv-alt-im-l: conv-alloc :state bins
            lv/lv-alt-re-r: conv-alloc :state bins
            lv/lv-alt-im-r: conv-alloc :state bins
            lv/lv-time: conv-vector :state (2 * size)
            lv/lv-play-l: conv-alloc :state size
            lv/lv-play-r: conv-alloc :state size
            lv/lv-play-alt-l: conv-alloc :state size
            lv/lv-play-alt-r: conv-alloc :state size
            lv/lv-build-l: conv-alloc :state size
            lv/lv-build-r: conv-alloc :state size
            lv/lv-build-alt-l: conv-alloc :state size
            lv/lv-build-alt-r: conv-alloc :state size
        ]
    ]
    return raw
]

brom-conv-destroy: func [
    "Release a convolver made by brom-conv-create."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Owned convolver; null is ignored."
    return: [none!]
] [
    if conv = as c-pointer! 0 [return none]
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    repeat index BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
        lv: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index)
        ; Raw buffers only: the plan and the vectors go with the store below.
        if lv/lv-max-parts > 0 [
            conv-free lv/lv-frame-l
            conv-free lv/lv-frame-r
            conv-free lv/lv-fdl-re-l
            conv-free lv/lv-fdl-im-l
            conv-free lv/lv-fdl-re-r
            conv-free lv/lv-fdl-im-r
            conv-free lv/lv-h-re-0
            conv-free lv/lv-h-im-0
            conv-free lv/lv-h-re-1
            conv-free lv/lv-h-im-1
            conv-free lv/lv-acc-re-l
            conv-free lv/lv-acc-im-l
            conv-free lv/lv-acc-re-r
            conv-free lv/lv-acc-im-r
            conv-free lv/lv-alt-re-l
            conv-free lv/lv-alt-im-l
            conv-free lv/lv-alt-re-r
            conv-free lv/lv-alt-im-r
            conv-free lv/lv-play-l
            conv-free lv/lv-play-r
            conv-free lv/lv-play-alt-l
            conv-free lv/lv-play-alt-r
            conv-free lv/lv-build-l
            conv-free lv/lv-build-r
            conv-free lv/lv-build-alt-l
            conv-free lv/lv-build-alt-r
        ]
    ]
    ; Last, since the records live in it: every plan and vector is released.
    conv-release state/cv-level-store
    state/cv-level-store: as c-pointer! 0
    state/cv-levels: as c-pointer! 0
    conv-free state/cv-head-0
    conv-free state/cv-head-1
    conv-free state/cv-hist-l
    conv-free state/cv-hist-r
    unsafe/free conv
]

brom-conv-capacity: func [
    "Longest response the convolver accepts."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    return: [i32!] "Capacity in taps."
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    return state/cv-capacity
]

brom-conv-memory-bytes: func [
    "Bytes the convolver allocated for its buffers."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    return: [i64!] "Total, excluding FFT plans and records."
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    return state/cv-bytes
]

brom-conv-length: func [
    "Length of the response currently being heard."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    return: [i32!] "Taps; zero before any response was staged. During a crossover, the longer of the two."
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    live: either state/cv-set = 0 [state/cv-length-0] [state/cv-length-1]
    if not state/cv-pending [return live]
    spare: either state/cv-set = 0 [state/cv-length-1] [state/cv-length-0]
    return either spare > live [spare] [live]
]

brom-conv-busy: func [
    "Whether a response is being staged or crossed over to, so a new one cannot start yet."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    return: [logic!] "True while staging or crossing over."
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    return any [state/cv-staging state/cv-pending]
]

brom-conv-staging: func [
    "Whether a staged response is still being transformed."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    return: [logic!] "True until brom-conv-stage-step has transformed every partition."
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    return state/cv-staging
]

brom-conv-reset: func [
    "Silence the convolver: clear every input history, delay line and pending output. The live response is kept."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    return: [none!]
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    conv-clear state/cv-hist-l (2 * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    conv-clear state/cv-hist-r (2 * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    state/cv-hist-pos: 0
    state/cv-tick-pos: 0
    repeat index BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
        lv: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index)
        parts: lv/lv-max-parts
        if parts > 0 [
            size: lv/lv-size
            bins: lv/lv-bins
            conv-clear lv/lv-frame-l (2 * size)
            conv-clear lv/lv-frame-r (2 * size)
            conv-clear lv/lv-fdl-re-l (parts * bins)
            conv-clear lv/lv-fdl-im-l (parts * bins)
            conv-clear lv/lv-fdl-re-r (parts * bins)
            conv-clear lv/lv-fdl-im-r (parts * bins)
            conv-clear lv/lv-play-l size
            conv-clear lv/lv-play-r size
            conv-clear lv/lv-play-alt-l size
            conv-clear lv/lv-play-alt-r size
            conv-clear lv/lv-build-l size
            conv-clear lv/lv-build-r size
            conv-clear lv/lv-build-alt-l size
            conv-clear lv/lv-build-alt-r size
            lv/lv-fdl-head: 0
            lv/lv-pos: 0
            lv/lv-tick: 0
            lv/lv-units: 0
            lv/lv-done: 0
            lv/lv-phase: CONV-PHASE-STEADY
        ]
    ]
]

brom-conv-clear: func [
    "Silence the convolver and forget its response, abandoning any staging or crossover, so the next response staged is taken at once instead of faded to. For a host's activate, which builds a new response before audio starts; not while the audio thread is processing."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    return: [none!]
] [
    brom-conv-reset :conv
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    state/cv-staging: false
    state/cv-pending: false
    state/cv-head-fade: 0
    state/cv-length-0: 0
    state/cv-length-1: 0
    conv-clear state/cv-head-0 (4 * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    conv-clear state/cv-head-1 (4 * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    ; Every level back on the live set with nothing pending, as after create.
    repeat index BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
        lv: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index)
        lv/lv-set: state/cv-set
        lv/lv-switched: true
    ]
]

; --- staging ----------------------------------------------------------------

brom-conv-stage-begin: func [
    "Start staging a new response into the spare set. The four sources are read, not copied, so they must stay valid and unchanged until brom-conv-staging turns false."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    :ll [c-pointer!] "Borrowed L->L taps, or null for a silent path."
    :lr [c-pointer!] "Borrowed L->R taps, or null."
    :rl [c-pointer!] "Borrowed R->L taps, or null."
    :rr [c-pointer!] "Borrowed R->R taps, or null."
    length [i32!] "Taps per path; clamped to the capacity."
    gain [f64!] "Linear gain applied to every tap as it is staged."
    return: [logic!] "False while a previous response is still staging or crossing over."
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    if any [state/cv-staging state/cv-pending] [return false]
    taps: make [#mutable i32!] length
    if taps < 0 [taps: 0]
    if taps > state/cv-capacity [taps: state/cv-capacity]
    state/cv-src-ll: ll
    state/cv-src-lr: lr
    state/cv-src-rl: rl
    state/cv-src-rr: rr
    state/cv-src-length: taps
    state/cv-src-gain: gain
    state/cv-stage-level: -1
    state/cv-stage-path: 0
    state/cv-stage-part: 0
    state/cv-staging: true
    return true
]

conv-source: func [
    #inline
    "The staged source buffer for one path."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    path [i32!] "BROM-CONV-LL .. BROM-CONV-RR."
    return: [c-pointer!] "Borrowed source, possibly null."
] [
    if path = BROM-CONV-LL [return state/cv-src-ll]
    if path = BROM-CONV-LR [return state/cv-src-lr]
    if path = BROM-CONV-RL [return state/cv-src-rl]
    return state/cv-src-rr
]

conv-stage-head: func [
    "Copy the first BROM-CONV-HEAD taps of every path, reversed and scaled, into the spare head set."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    return: [none!]
] [
    head: either state/cv-set = 0 [state/cv-head-1] [state/cv-head-0]
    gain: state/cv-src-gain
    taps: state/cv-src-length
    repeat path 4 [
        src: conv-source :state path
        repeat j BROM-CONV-HEAD [
            tap: BROM-CONV-HEAD - 1 - j
            value: either any [src = as c-pointer! 0 tap >= taps] [0.0] [gain * (conv-get :src tap)]
            conv-put :head ((path * BROM-CONV-HEAD) + j) value
        ]
    ]
]

conv-forward: func [
    "Forward-transform a 2P time frame into a spectrum slot of lv-bins real and imaginary parts."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    :input [vector! [f64!]] "Borrowed 2P time frame."
    :dest-re [c-pointer!] "Borrowed slot for the real parts."
    :dest-im [c-pointer!] "Borrowed slot for the imaginary parts."
    return: [none!]
] [
    bytes: lv/lv-bins * 8
    plan: lv/lv-plan
    spec-re: lv/lv-spec-re
    spec-im: lv/lv-spec-im
    rfft-forward :plan :input :spec-re :spec-im
    unsafe/memcpy dest-re spec-re/data bytes
    unsafe/memcpy dest-im spec-im/data bytes
    return none
]

conv-stage-partition: func [
    "Transform one partition of one path into the spare set."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    path [i32!] "BROM-CONV-LL .. BROM-CONV-RR."
    part [i32!] "Partition index inside the level."
    return: [none!]
] [
    size: lv/lv-size
    bins: lv/lv-bins
    time-vec: lv/lv-time
    time: time-vec/data
    src: conv-source :state path
    gain: state/cv-src-gain
    taps: state/cv-src-length
    ; Not called `first`: once any module of the build imports std/string,
    ; even only `find`, a local `first` here is compiled as a call to
    ; std/string's `first` (a Recoil compiler bug, T4108 with no location).
    first-tap: lv/lv-offset + (part * size)
    conv-clear time (2 * size)
    if src <> as c-pointer! 0 [
        repeat j size [
            tap: first-tap + j
            if tap < taps [conv-put :time j (gain * (conv-get :src tap))]
        ]
    ]
    spare-re: either state/cv-set = 0 [lv/lv-h-re-1] [lv/lv-h-re-0]
    spare-im: either state/cv-set = 0 [lv/lv-h-im-1] [lv/lv-h-im-0]
    slot: ((path * lv/lv-max-parts) + part) * bins
    conv-forward :lv :time-vec (conv-at :spare-re slot) (conv-at :spare-im slot)
]

brom-conv-stage-step: func [
    "Transform staged partitions until roughly `budget` FFT points have been spent. Call once per block from the audio thread; when the last partition is done, the response starts crossing over."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    budget [i32!] "FFT points to spend; at least one partition is always transformed."
    return: [logic!] "True when staging has finished (including on this call)."
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    if not state/cv-staging [return true]
    spent: make [#mutable i32!] 0
    if state/cv-stage-level < 0 [
        conv-stage-head :state
        state/cv-stage-level: 0
        spent: BROM-CONV-HEAD * 4
    ]
    while [state/cv-stage-level < BROM-CONV-LEVELS] [
        lv: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state state/cv-stage-level)
        parts: conv-parts-for state/cv-stage-level state/cv-src-length
        if any [state/cv-stage-part >= parts lv/lv-max-parts = 0] [
            state/cv-stage-part: 0
            state/cv-stage-path: state/cv-stage-path + 1
            if any [state/cv-stage-path >= 4 parts = 0] [
                state/cv-stage-path: 0
                state/cv-stage-level: state/cv-stage-level + 1
            ]
            continue
        ]
        if spent >= budget [return false]
        conv-stage-partition :state :lv state/cv-stage-path state/cv-stage-part
        spent: spent + (2 * lv/lv-size)
        state/cv-stage-part: state/cv-stage-part + 1
    ]
    ; Every partition is in the spare set. Record its extent, then hand it to
    ; the levels, which cross over one by one at their own boundaries.
    spare-length: state/cv-src-length
    either state/cv-set = 0 [state/cv-length-1: spare-length] [state/cv-length-0: spare-length]
    live-length: either state/cv-set = 0 [state/cv-length-0] [state/cv-length-1]
    repeat index BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
        lv2: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index)
        ; A level neither response reaches has nothing to fade, so it crosses
        ; over at once instead of holding the swap for a whole block of its
        ; own -- which for the top level would be 65536 samples of waiting.
        idle: all [
            (conv-parts-for index live-length) = 0
            (conv-parts-for index spare-length) = 0
        ]
        lv2/lv-switched: any [lv2/lv-max-parts = 0 idle]
        if all [lv2/lv-max-parts > 0 idle] [lv2/lv-set: 1 - lv2/lv-set]
    ]
    state/cv-staging: false
    ; Nothing is heard yet, so there is nothing to fade from: take the new
    ; response at once. This is what makes the first load immediate.
    if live-length = 0 [
        repeat index3 BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
            lv3: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index3)
            if not lv3/lv-switched [lv3/lv-set: 1 - lv3/lv-set]
            lv3/lv-switched: true
        ]
        state/cv-set: 1 - state/cv-set
        state/cv-pending: false
        state/cv-head-fade: 0
        return true
    ]
    state/cv-pending: true
    state/cv-head-fade: BROM-CONV-HEAD-FADE
    return true
]

; --- block work -------------------------------------------------------------

conv-set-parts: func [
    "Partitions in use by one set at one level."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    index [i32!] "Level index."
    set [i32!] "Set 0 or 1."
    return: [i32!] "Partition count."
] [
    length: either set = 0 [state/cv-length-0] [state/cv-length-1]
    return conv-parts-for index length
]

conv-mac: func [
    "Accumulate one partition's contribution for both outputs: acc_o += X_L[slot] H_L->o[part] + X_R[slot] H_R->o[part]."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    set [i32!] "Partition set 0 or 1."
    part [i32!] "Partition index."
    alt [logic!] "Accumulate into the -alt accumulators instead."
    return: [none!]
] [
    bins: lv/lv-bins
    parts: lv/lv-max-parts
    raw-slot: lv/lv-fdl-head - part
    slot: either raw-slot < 0 [raw-slot + parts] [raw-slot]
    x-off: slot * bins
    xlr: conv-at lv/lv-fdl-re-l x-off
    xli: conv-at lv/lv-fdl-im-l x-off
    xrr: conv-at lv/lv-fdl-re-r x-off
    xri: conv-at lv/lv-fdl-im-r x-off
    h-re: either set = 0 [lv/lv-h-re-0] [lv/lv-h-re-1]
    h-im: either set = 0 [lv/lv-h-im-0] [lv/lv-h-im-1]
    ll-off: ((BROM-CONV-LL * parts) + part) * bins
    lr-off: ((BROM-CONV-LR * parts) + part) * bins
    rl-off: ((BROM-CONV-RL * parts) + part) * bins
    rr-off: ((BROM-CONV-RR * parts) + part) * bins
    hllr: conv-at :h-re ll-off
    hlli: conv-at :h-im ll-off
    hlrr: conv-at :h-re lr-off
    hlri: conv-at :h-im lr-off
    hrlr: conv-at :h-re rl-off
    hrli: conv-at :h-im rl-off
    hrrr: conv-at :h-re rr-off
    hrri: conv-at :h-im rr-off
    acc-lr: either alt [lv/lv-alt-re-l] [lv/lv-acc-re-l]
    acc-li: either alt [lv/lv-alt-im-l] [lv/lv-acc-im-l]
    acc-rr: either alt [lv/lv-alt-re-r] [lv/lv-acc-re-r]
    acc-ri: either alt [lv/lv-alt-im-r] [lv/lv-acc-im-r]
    repeat k bins [
        a-r: conv-get :xlr k
        a-i: conv-get :xli k
        b-r: conv-get :xrr k
        b-i: conv-get :xri k
        p-r: conv-get :hllr k
        p-i: conv-get :hlli k
        q-r: conv-get :hrlr k
        q-i: conv-get :hrli k
        conv-put :acc-lr k ((conv-get :acc-lr k) + (((a-r * p-r) - (a-i * p-i)) + ((b-r * q-r) - (b-i * q-i))))
        conv-put :acc-li k ((conv-get :acc-li k) + (((a-r * p-i) + (a-i * p-r)) + ((b-r * q-i) + (b-i * q-r))))
        s-r: conv-get :hlrr k
        s-i: conv-get :hlri k
        t-r: conv-get :hrrr k
        t-i: conv-get :hrri k
        conv-put :acc-rr k ((conv-get :acc-rr k) + (((a-r * s-r) - (a-i * s-i)) + ((b-r * t-r) - (b-i * t-i))))
        conv-put :acc-ri k ((conv-get :acc-ri k) + (((a-r * s-i) + (a-i * s-r)) + ((b-r * t-i) + (b-i * t-r))))
    ]
]

conv-inverse: func [
    "Inverse-transform one accumulator into a build buffer, keeping the valid last half of the overlap-save frame."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    :acc-re [c-pointer!] "Borrowed accumulator real parts."
    :acc-im [c-pointer!] "Borrowed accumulator imaginary parts."
    :dest [c-pointer!] "Borrowed lv-size output buffer."
    return: [none!]
] [
    size: lv/lv-size
    bytes: lv/lv-bins * 8
    plan: lv/lv-plan
    time-vec: lv/lv-time
    time: time-vec/data
    spec-re: lv/lv-spec-re
    spec-im: lv/lv-spec-im
    ; The inverse runs inside the spectrum it is given, so it gets a copy
    ; and the accumulator is left as it was.
    unsafe/memcpy spec-re/data acc-re bytes
    unsafe/memcpy spec-im/data acc-im bytes
    rfft-inverse :plan :spec-re :spec-im :time-vec
    unsafe/memcpy dest (conv-at :time size) (size * 8)
    return none
]

; The snapshot is bound in a helper of its own, in a straight-line body: a
; vector bound inside a block that returns early is not released, and an
; `either` choosing between two vector fields retains both and releases one,
; so either form in conv-run-unit would leave a reference behind per call.
conv-forward-left: func [
    "Transform the left snapshot into the left delay-line slot at `x-off`."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    x-off [i32!] "Element offset of the slot in the delay line."
    return: [none!]
] [
    snap: lv/lv-snap-l
    conv-forward :lv :snap (conv-at lv/lv-fdl-re-l x-off) (conv-at lv/lv-fdl-im-l x-off)
]

conv-forward-right: func [
    "Transform the right snapshot into the right delay-line slot at `x-off`."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    x-off [i32!] "Element offset of the slot in the delay line."
    return: [none!]
] [
    snap: lv/lv-snap-r
    conv-forward :lv :snap (conv-at lv/lv-fdl-re-r x-off) (conv-at lv/lv-fdl-im-r x-off)
]

conv-unit-count: func [
    "Work units in one block for a level: two forward FFTs, the MACs, and the inverse FFTs, doubled for a DUAL block."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    index [i32!] "Level index."
    return: [i32!] "Unit count."
] [
    live-parts: conv-set-parts :state index lv/lv-set
    if lv/lv-phase = CONV-PHASE-DUAL [
        other-parts: conv-set-parts :state index (1 - lv/lv-set)
        return 2 + live-parts + other-parts + 4
    ]
    return 2 + live-parts + 2
]

conv-run-unit: func [
    "Perform work unit `unit` of the current block for a level."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    index [i32!] "Level index."
    unit [i32!] "Unit number in 0 .. conv-unit-count - 1."
    return: [none!]
] [
    bins: lv/lv-bins
    x-off: lv/lv-fdl-head * bins
    dual: lv/lv-phase = CONV-PHASE-DUAL
    live: lv/lv-set
    live-parts: conv-set-parts :state index live
    other-parts: either dual [conv-set-parts :state index (1 - live)] [0]
    mac-end: 2 + live-parts + other-parts
    if unit = 0 [
        ; Clear the accumulators for this block, then transform the left
        ; input frame into the delay-line slot the boundary advanced to.
        conv-clear lv/lv-acc-re-l bins
        conv-clear lv/lv-acc-im-l bins
        conv-clear lv/lv-acc-re-r bins
        conv-clear lv/lv-acc-im-r bins
        conv-clear lv/lv-alt-re-l bins
        conv-clear lv/lv-alt-im-l bins
        conv-clear lv/lv-alt-re-r bins
        conv-clear lv/lv-alt-im-r bins
        conv-forward-left :lv x-off
        return none
    ]
    if unit = 1 [
        conv-forward-right :lv x-off
        return none
    ]
    if unit < (2 + live-parts) [
        conv-mac :lv live (unit - 2) false
        return none
    ]
    if unit < mac-end [
        conv-mac :lv (1 - live) (unit - 2 - live-parts) true
        return none
    ]
    step: unit - mac-end
    if step = 0 [conv-inverse :lv lv/lv-acc-re-l lv/lv-acc-im-l lv/lv-build-l]
    if step = 1 [conv-inverse :lv lv/lv-acc-re-r lv/lv-acc-im-r lv/lv-build-r]
    if step = 2 [conv-inverse :lv lv/lv-alt-re-l lv/lv-alt-im-l lv/lv-build-alt-l]
    if step = 3 [conv-inverse :lv lv/lv-alt-re-r lv/lv-alt-im-r lv/lv-build-alt-r]
]

conv-boundary: func [
    "Start a new block for a level: advance the crossover phase, promote the built output to playing, snapshot the input frame and reset the scheduler."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    index [i32!] "Level index."
    return: [none!]
] [
    size: lv/lv-size
    ; Crossover bookkeeping first: it decides what the outputs built during the
    ; block that just ended mean.
    if lv/lv-phase = CONV-PHASE-FADE [
        lv/lv-phase: CONV-PHASE-STEADY
        lv/lv-switched: true
    ]
    if lv/lv-phase = CONV-PHASE-DUAL [
        ; Last block computed both; play them faded, and from now on compute
        ; with the new set only.
        lv/lv-phase: CONV-PHASE-FADE
        lv/lv-set: 1 - lv/lv-set
    ]
    if all [lv/lv-phase = CONV-PHASE-STEADY state/cv-pending not lv/lv-switched] [
        lv/lv-phase: CONV-PHASE-DUAL
    ]
    ; Promote: the block built last period plays now.
    old-play-l: lv/lv-play-l
    old-play-r: lv/lv-play-r
    lv/lv-play-l: lv/lv-build-l
    lv/lv-play-r: lv/lv-build-r
    lv/lv-build-l: old-play-l
    lv/lv-build-r: old-play-r
    old-alt-l: lv/lv-play-alt-l
    old-alt-r: lv/lv-play-alt-r
    lv/lv-play-alt-l: lv/lv-build-alt-l
    lv/lv-play-alt-r: lv/lv-build-alt-r
    lv/lv-build-alt-l: old-alt-l
    lv/lv-build-alt-r: old-alt-r
    ; In FADE the alt pair holds the new set's output and the main pair the
    ; old one -- but the live set has already flipped, so swap them so the
    ; main pair is always "live" and alt is always "the other".
    if lv/lv-phase = CONV-PHASE-FADE [
        main-l: lv/lv-play-l
        main-r: lv/lv-play-r
        lv/lv-play-l: lv/lv-play-alt-l
        lv/lv-play-r: lv/lv-play-alt-r
        lv/lv-play-alt-l: main-l
        lv/lv-play-alt-r: main-r
    ]
    ; Snapshot the frame and slide it by one block.
    frame-l: lv/lv-frame-l
    frame-r: lv/lv-frame-r
    snap-l: lv/lv-snap-l
    snap-r: lv/lv-snap-r
    unsafe/memcpy snap-l/data frame-l (2 * size * 8)
    unsafe/memcpy snap-r/data frame-r (2 * size * 8)
    unsafe/memcpy frame-l (conv-at :frame-l size) (size * 8)
    unsafe/memcpy frame-r (conv-at :frame-r size) (size * 8)
    next-head: lv/lv-fdl-head + 1
    lv/lv-fdl-head: either next-head >= lv/lv-max-parts [0] [next-head]
    lv/lv-pos: 0
    lv/lv-tick: 0
    lv/lv-done: 0
    lv/lv-units: conv-unit-count :state :lv index
]

conv-tick: func [
    "Run this tick's share of a level's block work."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    index [i32!] "Level index."
    return: [none!]
] [
    ticks: lv/lv-ticks
    units: lv/lv-units
    target: ((lv/lv-tick + 1) * units) / ticks
    while [lv/lv-done < target] [
        conv-run-unit :state :lv index lv/lv-done
        lv/lv-done: lv/lv-done + 1
    ]
    lv/lv-tick: lv/lv-tick + 1
]

conv-finish-crossover: func [
    "Retire the pending response once every level and the head have crossed over to it."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    return: [none!]
] [
    if not state/cv-pending [return none]
    if state/cv-head-fade > 0 [return none]
    repeat index BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
        lv: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index)
        if not lv/lv-switched [return none]
    ]
    state/cv-set: 1 - state/cv-set
    state/cv-pending: false
]

conv-head-out: func [
    #inline
    "One output channel of the direct-form head: taps of path `from-l` against the left window plus taps of `from-r` against the right."
    :head [c-pointer!] "Borrowed head set: 4 paths of reversed taps."
    from-l [i32!] "Path from the left input to this output."
    from-r [i32!] "Path from the right input to this output."
    :win-l [c-pointer!] "Borrowed oldest-first window of the last HEAD left inputs."
    :win-r [c-pointer!] "Borrowed oldest-first window of the last HEAD right inputs."
    return: [f64!] "The head's output for this sample."
] [
    taps-l: conv-at :head (from-l * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    taps-r: conv-at :head (from-r * BROM-CONV-HEAD)
    ; Four independent sums rather than one: a single accumulator makes
    ; every multiply-add wait for the previous add, and this loop runs 256
    ; times per output sample.
    a0: make [#mutable f64!] 0.0
    a1: make [#mutable f64!] 0.0
    b0: make [#mutable f64!] 0.0
    b1: make [#mutable f64!] 0.0
    repeat half (BROM-CONV-HEAD / 2) [
        j: half * 2
        k: j + 1
        a0: a0 + ((conv-get :taps-l j) * (conv-get :win-l j))
        a1: a1 + ((conv-get :taps-l k) * (conv-get :win-l k))
        b0: b0 + ((conv-get :taps-r j) * (conv-get :win-r j))
        b1: b1 + ((conv-get :taps-r k) * (conv-get :win-r k))
    ]
    return (a0 + a1) + (b0 + b1)
]

conv-feed-level: func [
    "Copy a run of input into a level's frame, at its current block position."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    :in-l [c-pointer!] "Borrowed left input run."
    :in-r [c-pointer!] "Borrowed right input run."
    count [i32!] "Samples in the run; never crosses the level's block end."
    return: [none!]
] [
    write-at: lv/lv-size + lv/lv-pos
    unsafe/memcpy (conv-at lv/lv-frame-l write-at) in-l (count * 8)
    unsafe/memcpy (conv-at lv/lv-frame-r write-at) in-r (count * 8)
    return none
]

conv-play-level: func [
    "Add a run of a level's playing output into the outputs, fading old to new during a crossover, and advance its position."
    :lv [conv-level!] "Borrowed level record."
    :out-l [c-pointer!] "Borrowed left output run, accumulated into."
    :out-r [c-pointer!] "Borrowed right output run, accumulated into."
    count [i32!] "Samples in the run."
    return: [none!]
] [
    p: lv/lv-pos
    play-l: conv-at lv/lv-play-l p
    play-r: conv-at lv/lv-play-r p
    either lv/lv-phase = CONV-PHASE-FADE [
        ; Main is the new set, alt the old one.
        alt-l: conv-at lv/lv-play-alt-l p
        alt-r: conv-at lv/lv-play-alt-r p
        inv-size: 1.0 / (as f64! lv/lv-size)
        repeat i count [
            g: ((as f64! (p + i)) + 0.5) * inv-size
            h: 1.0 - g
            conv-put :out-l i ((conv-get :out-l i) + (((conv-get :play-l i) * g) + ((conv-get :alt-l i) * h)))
            conv-put :out-r i ((conv-get :out-r i) + (((conv-get :play-r i) * g) + ((conv-get :alt-r i) * h)))
        ]
    ] [
        repeat i count [
            conv-put :out-l i ((conv-get :out-l i) + (conv-get :play-l i))
            conv-put :out-r i ((conv-get :out-r i) + (conv-get :play-r i))
        ]
    ]
    lv/lv-pos: p + count
    return none
]

conv-head-run: func [
    "Run the direct-form head over a run of input, writing (not adding) the outputs."
    :state [conv-state!] "Borrowed convolver state."
    :in-l [c-pointer!] "Borrowed left input run."
    :in-r [c-pointer!] "Borrowed right input run."
    :out-l [c-pointer!] "Borrowed left output run; may alias in-l."
    :out-r [c-pointer!] "Borrowed right output run; may alias in-r."
    count [i32!] "Samples in the run."
    return: [none!]
] [
    hist-l: state/cv-hist-l
    hist-r: state/cv-hist-r
    live-head: either state/cv-set = 0 [state/cv-head-0] [state/cv-head-1]
    new-head: either state/cv-set = 0 [state/cv-head-1] [state/cv-head-0]
    ; While a response is pending the head fades to it, then stays on it
    ; until the slowest level has crossed over and the sets swap.
    on-new: all [state/cv-pending state/cv-head-fade = 0]
    heard-head: either on-new [new-head] [live-head]
    repeat n count [
        x-l: conv-get :in-l n
        x-r: conv-get :in-r n
        ; The history is written at pos and pos + HEAD, so the last HEAD
        ; samples always sit contiguously at pos + 1 .. pos + HEAD.
        pos: state/cv-hist-pos
        conv-put :hist-l pos x-l
        conv-put :hist-l (pos + BROM-CONV-HEAD) x-l
        conv-put :hist-r pos x-r
        conv-put :hist-r (pos + BROM-CONV-HEAD) x-r
        win-l: conv-at :hist-l (pos + 1)
        win-r: conv-at :hist-r (pos + 1)
        y-l: make [#mutable f64!] conv-head-out :heard-head BROM-CONV-LL BROM-CONV-RL :win-l :win-r
        y-r: make [#mutable f64!] conv-head-out :heard-head BROM-CONV-LR BROM-CONV-RR :win-l :win-r
        if all [state/cv-pending state/cv-head-fade > 0] [
            n-l: conv-head-out :new-head BROM-CONV-LL BROM-CONV-RL :win-l :win-r
            n-r: conv-head-out :new-head BROM-CONV-LR BROM-CONV-RR :win-l :win-r
            g: 1.0 - ((as f64! state/cv-head-fade) / (as f64! BROM-CONV-HEAD-FADE))
            y-l: (y-l * (1.0 - g)) + (n-l * g)
            y-r: (y-r * (1.0 - g)) + (n-r * g)
            state/cv-head-fade: state/cv-head-fade - 1
        ]
        next-pos: pos + 1
        state/cv-hist-pos: either next-pos >= BROM-CONV-HEAD [0] [next-pos]
        conv-put :out-l n y-l
        conv-put :out-r n y-r
    ]
    return none
]

brom-conv-process: func [
    "Convolve `frames` samples of stereo input. Writes the wet signal only; mix it with the dry signal yourself."
    :conv [c-pointer!] "Borrowed convolver."
    :in-l [c-pointer!] "Borrowed left input, `frames` f64."
    :in-r [c-pointer!] "Borrowed right input, `frames` f64."
    :out-l [c-pointer!] "Borrowed left output, `frames` f64; may alias in-l."
    :out-r [c-pointer!] "Borrowed right output, `frames` f64; may alias in-r."
    frames [i32!] "Samples to process."
    return: [none!]
] [
    state: make [#mutable conv-state!] as conv-state! conv
    done: make [#mutable i32!] 0
    ; Work in runs that end at the next tick, so every level is handled once
    ; per run instead of once per sample.
    while [done < frames] [
        room: BROM-CONV-TICK - state/cv-tick-pos
        left: frames - done
        count: either left < room [left] [room]
        run-in-l: conv-at :in-l done
        run-in-r: conv-at :in-r done
        run-out-l: conv-at :out-l done
        run-out-r: conv-at :out-r done
        ; Feed the levels before the head writes the outputs, because the
        ; outputs may be the inputs.
        repeat index BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
            lv: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index)
            if lv/lv-max-parts > 0 [conv-feed-level :lv :run-in-l :run-in-r count]
        ]
        conv-head-run :state :run-in-l :run-in-r :run-out-l :run-out-r count
        repeat index2 BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
            lv2: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index2)
            if lv2/lv-max-parts > 0 [conv-play-level :lv2 :run-out-l :run-out-r count]
        ]
        done: done + count
        tick-next: state/cv-tick-pos + count
        state/cv-tick-pos: either tick-next >= BROM-CONV-TICK [0] [tick-next]
        ; Tick: after the sample that completes one.
        if state/cv-tick-pos = 0 [
            repeat index3 BROM-CONV-LEVELS [
                lv3: make [#mutable conv-level!] as conv-level! (conv-level-view :state index3)
                if lv3/lv-max-parts > 0 [
                    if lv3/lv-pos >= lv3/lv-size [conv-boundary :state :lv3 index3]
                    conv-tick :state :lv3 index3
                ]
            ]
            conv-finish-crossover :state
        ]
    ]
]
